WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.113
- We can't roll the credit

00:00:01.113 --> 00:00:02.940
to that one last feel
good story to hopefully

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.320
bring you a little extra joy.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.520
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.570
It's Asian American and
Pacific Islander Heritage Month

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:12.403
here in the US.

00:00:12.403 --> 00:00:14.100
And a group of artists in Atlanta have

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.370
collaborated to ensure kids know

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.130
about the profound contributions

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.990
the AAPI community has made to

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.830
American culture and history.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:26.440
They put out a coloring book
called the ABCs of AAPIs

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.330
and it features an extensive collection

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:29.560
of influential figures.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:31.370
We have the co-creative director

00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:33.240
for the project on the line right now.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.420
Everybody let's say hi to
Kavi watching on WSBTV!

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:38.410
Hi.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.400
(audience applause)

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.233
- Hi Kelly.

00:00:41.233 --> 00:00:43.080
It's so good to meet you.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.330
- It's nice to meet you as well.

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.130
First of all, you look like
you're in a very cool place.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:48.429
I like that brick wall with
all that little neon going on

00:00:48.429 --> 00:00:51.470
looks like a cool bar or really cool pad.

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:53.850
So, so how did, how did the idea

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.430
for the coloring book come about?

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:57.090
- So I am a videographer

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.214
and creative consultant with
Asian American Advocacy Fund

00:01:00.214 --> 00:01:03.060
and we were lucky enough
to get a grant to work

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.770
with Asian American artists in the

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:08.060
area to advance some social issue.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.819
So we did a brainstorming session with

00:01:09.819 --> 00:01:11.900
dozens of artists in Atlanta,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:14.539
and we asked them basically what is it

00:01:14.539 --> 00:01:18.000
that you wanted to make or see growing up?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.950
And the AAPI community, we've been

00:01:19.950 --> 00:01:22.430
through a lot these past two years.

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:25.710
So we wanted to make
something that was healing

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:29.400
and felt community driven,
but also celebratory

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.250
for our heritage and AAPI Heritage Month.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.230
So we figured the ABCs
of AAPIs coloring book

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:37.650
would do just that.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.850
And we engaged with different
student organizations to

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.989
research this huge list of
influential Asian figures.

00:01:43.989 --> 00:01:47.137
And we wanted to also add experiences that

00:01:47.137 --> 00:01:49.474
felt true to our culture.

00:01:49.474 --> 00:01:50.670
- I love that.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:52.210
So you've actually gotten support

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.560
from people featured in
the book as well, right?

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.270
- Absolutely. And it has felt so surreal

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:01.090
for that because K is for Michelle Kwan.

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:02.871
- Kwan, yeah.
- And I mean, I grew up

00:02:02.871 --> 00:02:05.730
watching Michelle and, you know

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.470
feeling so represented
when she won the Olympics

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.499
and we tagged her in an Instagram story

00:02:10.499 --> 00:02:12.810
and she responded and she was like,

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:14.160
can I, can I have a book?

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.994
And we're like, you can have
as many books as you want.

00:02:16.994 --> 00:02:19.335
And there are poetry passages as well

00:02:19.335 --> 00:02:21.311
to give context to the figures.

00:02:21.311 --> 00:02:25.010
And we've gotten so much
community support as well.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:28.950
So in fact there is 150 foot display

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:33.100
of our coloring book in all
color on the Atlanta belt line

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.160
which is this huge pedestrian friendly

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:39.550
and biker friendly pathway
all across the city.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:43.950
And it's just so affirming
to see our art display

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.160
to thousands of people every day.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.060
We hope that you'll come see it.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.840
If you're in the area, it's
up until the end of June.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.210
- It is such a beautiful way
to educate everyone on people.

00:02:56.210 --> 00:02:59.330
Maybe they didn't know,
especially children seeing this.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:02.120
It's such a really cool
innovative way to do this.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:03.260
Way to go Kavi.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.093
This is really cool.

00:03:04.093 --> 00:03:06.563
I'm liking your post right now, alright?

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:08.790
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.100
- Alright and that's not all girl,

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.070
our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:03:13.070 --> 00:03:15.290
the go to pen of the Kelly Clarkson show.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.010
They wanna honor ultimate
overachievers just like you ma'am.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.715
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:03:19.715 --> 00:03:22.144
to the Asian American Advocacy Fund

00:03:22.144 --> 00:03:24.540
on your behalf for a thousand dollars.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.528
And... (audience applause)

00:03:26.528 --> 00:03:29.760
And I'm also gonna add
5,000 dollars to that

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:31.720
for a total of 6,000 dollars because

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.510
we think what you're doing is really rad.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.753
Thank you so much, Kavi!

